{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795360651,"nonce":"aP1/yAg74HiQtEkjCHopAhABLpA=","message":"Fix committed locally as b2f6730c (not pushed). Left open until it lands on origin/main.\n\nEvidence. Unfixed binary, hybrid, NaGap run 6 or 8 at a time: hl.Bytes at 1.7 ns per element in 2 of 360 and 1 of 800 runs; sequential runs never (0 of 400). Fixed binary, 8 at a time: 0 of 1600 slow Bytes runs. Two runs had the NativeArray loop at 0.31 and 0.38; their logs show the LLVM install at 32 ms and 35 ms, so that is scheduler noise from eight processes on ten cores.\n\nDeterministic reproducer: TestLoopsHot.hx (fixture test_loops_hot.hl). Before the fix the log has \"[loops] generation 1\" and the kernel never gets an LLVM install; after, \"[tier] loops propose\" and an install. The new test in loop_owner_promotion.rs checks the install. The other loop_owner_promotion tests, handoff_reentry, nested_strip, osr_retier, tree_fusion and value_array_gc pass on the Mac.\n\nNUC benchmark A/B, 13 benchmarks, hybrid-auto, 15 interleaved runs against the alignment commit da7a63b2: all deltas within the spread (largest free_call +4.6% at 5% spread, fib +3.2% at 14.5% spread). The new path fires on deltablue only among the nine bench programs I could map by name (8 loop proposals against 5 before; delta -0.1%); on the other eight the two binaries behave the same, so their deltas are the noise floor of that sweep. nbody, mandelbrot_small, stdlib and jsonparse were not counted for proposals. The NUC was shared with another build during the sweep, so absolute medians are 10 to 20% above earlier sweeps.\n\nNot covered: hxn's 0.1.21 observation of `--mode jit` giving NativeArray 1.70 once in two runs.","files":null}]}